      "reason": "The frozen configuration defines rotationsgroup as the literal R. Thus rotationsgroup_1 and R_1 print the identical already-defined notation. Sol6 compared TeX command names instead of their mathematical output; the undefined-index claim is a false positive. The rational-radian and rotation-domain defects are independent and remain disclosed."
    },
    "OLSTH-032": {
      "id": "OLSTH-032",
      "status": "superseded",
      "superseded_by": "SOL6_MEMBERSHIP_RECONCILIATION.json",
      "reason": "The source says any x in B is also in D and any x in C is also in E. The sentence supplies x as the subject of the inline relation fragment. A math span need not be a complete standalone formula. No membership defect or proof gap follows. Sol6 classified the fragments in isolation, and the adjacent target warning was misleading."
    },
    "OLSTH-033": {
      "id": "OLSTH-033",
      "reason": "The explanatory proof derives an existence claim from A neq emptyset, then prints x neq emptyset iff some x is in A. The left-hand subject must concern A for that equivalence; the printed x/A substitution is a source error. The target preserves the exact formula and gives an adjacent Pashto disclosure."
    }
  },
